# Session-Based Testing First: Test-Driven Development

## Purpose
Enforce strict test-driven development within each session where controller/integration tests are written before implementation, tests drive design decisions, and all tests must pass before session completion.

## Session TDD Core Principle

RED → GREEN → REFACTOR (per session)

1. RED: Write a test that fails (at session start)
2. GREEN: Implement minimum code to pass the test (during session)
3. REFACTOR: Improve code while keeping tests green (before session end)

## Session Testing Context

Each session follows TDD principles:
- Session N: Write `@WebMvcTest`/`@SpringBootTest` for the current endpoint
- Session N: Implement the endpoint to make tests pass
- Session N: Refactor while keeping tests green
- Session N: Document test results in session summary

## Test Layer Choice

| Layer | Annotation | DB | Speed | Use for |
|-------|-----------|----|----|---------|
| Controller (sliced) | `@WebMvcTest(Controller.class)` + `MockMvc` | Mocked (`@MockBean` on the service) | Fast | Verifying request/response mapping, validation, status codes |
| Full integration | `@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = RANDOM_PORT)` + `TestRestTemplate` | Real (Testcontainers) | Slower | End-to-end flow through controller → service → repository → Postgres |
| Service unit | `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` | Mocked (`@Mock` repository) | Fastest | Business logic branches, edge cases, without Spring context |
| Repository | `@DataJpaTest` or Testcontainers | Real | Medium | Query-method correctness, custom `@Query` |

## Controller Test Patterns (`@WebMvcTest`)

### Test Structure
Every endpoint test follows this structure:

```java
@WebMvcTest(PostController.class)
class PostControllerTest {

    @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc;
    @MockBean PostService postService;

    @Test
    void createPost_successCase() throws Exception { }

    @Test
    void createPost_errorCase_returns404WhenAuthorMissing() throws Exception { }

    @Test
    void createPost_validationCase_rejectsBlankTitle() throws Exception { }

    @Test
    void createPost_authenticationCase_returns401WithoutToken() throws Exception { }
}
```

### Using Skeleton Mock Data
Phase 0 skeleton provides the expected output structure.

**Step 1: Capture the mock response shape**
```java
// From Phase 0 skeleton
// POST /api/posts returns:
// {
//   "postId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000123",
//   "title": "Mock Resource",
//   "content": "Mock description",
//   "authorId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000aa",
//   "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
// }
```

**Step 2: Write test using that structure**
```java
@Test
void createPost_returnsCreatedPost() throws Exception {
    UUID authorId = UUID.randomUUID();
    Post saved = new Post();
    saved.setId(UUID.randomUUID());
    saved.setTitle("Test Resource");
    saved.setContent("Test description");
    saved.setAuthorId(authorId);
    saved.setCreatedAt(Instant.now());

    given(postService.createPost(any(), eq(authorId))).willReturn(saved);

    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content("""
                {"title":"Test Resource","content":"Test description","authorId":"%s"}
                """.formatted(authorId))
            .header("Authorization", "Bearer " + testToken))
        .andExpect(status().isOk())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.postId").exists())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.title").value("Test Resource"))
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.content").value("Test description"))
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.authorId").value(authorId.toString()))
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.createdAt").exists());
}
```

### Testing Patterns by HTTP Method

**POST Endpoints:**
```java
@Test
void createPost_success() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content(validPostJson)
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isOk())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.postId").isNotEmpty());
}

@Test
void createPost_validation_blankTitleReturns400() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content("""{"title":"","content":"x","authorId":"%s"}""".formatted(UUID.randomUUID()))
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}

@Test
void createPost_unauthorized_returns401() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content(validPostJson))
        .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
}
```

**GET Endpoints:**
```java
@Test
void getPost_success() throws Exception {
    UUID postId = UUID.randomUUID();
    given(postService.getPost(postId)).willReturn(Optional.of(existingPost));

    mockMvc.perform(get("/api/posts/{id}", postId)
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isOk())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.postId").value(postId.toString()));
}

@Test
void getPost_notFound_returns404() throws Exception {
    UUID missingId = UUID.randomUUID();
    given(postService.getPost(missingId)).willReturn(Optional.empty());

    mockMvc.perform(get("/api/posts/{id}", missingId)
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isNotFound());
}
```

**PUT/PATCH Endpoints:**
```java
@Test
void updatePost_success() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(put("/api/posts/{id}", postId)
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content("""{"title":"Updated Name"}""")
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isOk())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.title").value("Updated Name"));
}
```

**DELETE Endpoints:**
```java
@Test
void deletePost_success() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(delete("/api/posts/{id}", postId)
            .header("Authorization", authHeader))
        .andExpect(status().isNoContent());
}
```

## Unit Testing Patterns (Mockito)

Unit tests are written AFTER controller tests pass, to lock down service-layer edge cases.

### Service Layer Tests

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class PostServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private PostRepository postRepository;

    @InjectMocks
    private PostService postService;

    @Test
    void createPost_success() {
        UUID authorId = UUID.randomUUID();
        CreatePostRequest request = new CreatePostRequest("Test", "Description", authorId);
        Post saved = new Post();
        saved.setId(UUID.randomUUID());
        saved.setTitle("Test");
        saved.setAuthorId(authorId);

        when(postRepository.save(any(Post.class))).thenReturn(saved);

        Post result = postService.createPost(request, authorId);

        assertThat(result.getId()).isNotNull();
        assertThat(result.getTitle()).isEqualTo("Test");
        verify(postRepository).save(any(Post.class));
    }

    @Test
    void createPost_repositoryThrows_propagatesException() {
        UUID authorId = UUID.randomUUID();
        CreatePostRequest request = new CreatePostRequest("Test", "Description", authorId);
        when(postRepository.save(any(Post.class))).thenThrow(new DataIntegrityViolationException("db error"));

        assertThatThrownBy(() -> postService.createPost(request, authorId))
            .isInstanceOf(DataIntegrityViolationException.class);
    }
}
```

## Integration Testing with Testcontainers

Full-stack tests that exercise a real Postgres instance:

```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)
@Testcontainers
class PostIntegrationTest {

    @Container
    static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:15-alpine")
        .withDatabaseName("testdb")
        .withUsername("test")
        .withPassword("test");

    @DynamicPropertySource
    static void configureProperties(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
        registry.add("spring.datasource.url", postgres::getJdbcUrl);
        registry.add("spring.datasource.username", postgres::getUsername);
        registry.add("spring.datasource.password", postgres::getPassword);
    }

    @Autowired
    private TestRestTemplate restTemplate;

    @Autowired
    private PostRepository postRepository;

    @Test
    void createPost_persistsToDatabase() {
        UUID authorId = UUID.randomUUID();
        CreatePostRequest request = new CreatePostRequest("Integration Test", "Body", authorId);

        ResponseEntity<PostResponse> response = restTemplate.postForEntity(
            "/api/posts", request, PostResponse.class);

        assertThat(response.getStatusCode()).isEqualTo(HttpStatus.OK);
        assertThat(postRepository.findById(response.getBody().postId())).isPresent();
    }
}
```

`@Container` boots a real, ephemeral Postgres in Docker for the test class lifetime — no mocking of the datasource, no shared state between test runs, and the schema is created via the same Flyway migrations used in production.

## Test Organization

```
src/test/java/com/example/<app>/
├── web/                     # @WebMvcTest controller tests
│   ├── HealthControllerTest.java
│   └── PostControllerTest.java
├── service/                 # Mockito unit tests
│   └── PostServiceTest.java
├── integration/             # @SpringBootTest + Testcontainers
│   └── PostIntegrationTest.java
└── ApplicationTests.java    # context-loads smoke test
```

## Session Test Execution Strategy

### Session Development (TDD Cycle)
```bash
# Run a specific test class while implementing in the current session
./mvnw test -Dtest=PostControllerTest

# Run a specific test method
./mvnw test -Dtest=PostControllerTest#createPost_returnsCreatedPost
```

### Session Completion
```bash
# Run all tests for current session's package
./mvnw test -Dtest=com.example.app.web.PostControllerTest

# Run all tests to ensure no regressions
./mvnw test

# Run with coverage (jacoco)
./mvnw test jacoco:report
```

## Test Data Management

### Database State
For integration tests using a real (Testcontainers) database:
- Use randomly generated UUIDs to avoid collisions between tests
- Wrap tests in `@Transactional` (rolled back after each test) when full isolation is needed, or clean tables in `@AfterEach`
- Keep the Testcontainers instance scoped per test class (`static` field) for speed, not per method

### Mock Data Consistency
Use consistent patterns:
```java
static final UUID TEST_USER_ID = UUID.fromString("00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000aa");
static final UUID TEST_POST_ID = UUID.fromString("00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000123");
static final Instant TEST_TIMESTAMP = Instant.parse("2024-01-01T00:00:00Z");
```

## Assertions Best Practices

### Be Specific
```java
// Good: specific AssertJ assertions
assertThat(response.getBody().title()).isEqualTo("Expected Title");
assertThat(response.getBody().postId()).isNotNull();
assertThat(response.getBody().createdAt()).isInstanceOf(Instant.class);

// Bad: too generic
assertThat(response.getBody()).isNotNull();
```

### Test Error Messages
```java
// Good: verify ProblemDetail contents
mockMvc.perform(get("/api/posts/{id}", missingId))
    .andExpect(status().isNotFound())
    .andExpect(jsonPath("$.detail").value("Post not found"));

// Bad: only check status code
mockMvc.perform(get("/api/posts/{id}", missingId))
    .andExpect(status().isNotFound());
```

### Test Side Effects
```java
// Good: verify state changes via the repository, not just the response
mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")...).andExpect(status().isOk());
assertThat(postRepository.findAll()).hasSize(1);
```

## Session Testing Checklist

Before completing any session:

- [ ] Session plan reviewed and test objectives confirmed
- [ ] `@WebMvcTest`/`@SpringBootTest` written before implementation
- [ ] Test initially fails (proves it tests something)
- [ ] Test uses skeleton mock data structure
- [ ] All success cases tested for current endpoint
- [ ] All error cases tested for current endpoint
- [ ] Authentication tested
- [ ] Validation tested
- [ ] All tests passing for current endpoint
- [ ] Mockito unit tests added for complex business logic
- [ ] Test coverage adequate for new code
- [ ] Tests are maintainable and readable
- [ ] Session summary documents test results

## Session Testing Anti-Patterns

Do NOT:
- Skip session plan review
- Write implementation before test
- Skip a test because "it's simple"
- Test implementation details instead of behavior
- Use `Thread.sleep()` instead of Awaitility or proper synchronization
- Share mutable state between tests
- Forget to test error cases
- Test only the happy path
- Commit code with failing tests
- Skip tests during "rapid development"
- Test endpoints from other sessions
- Skip session test documentation
